ific claim you've been defending—that equatorial climate makes a national population inherently less sharp—is unsupported by those differences and contradicted by what we know about human adaptability. If you want to argue that Ecuador currently has lower average educational outcomes than some other nations, that's a measurable fact. If you want to argue that this means Ecuadorians are biologically less intelligent, you've left the data behind and entered the realm of assumption dressed as conclusion. That's the leap I'm asking you to examine.
